<Layout title="FilePebble privacy — Local processing explained">
  <article class="prose-page wrap"><div class="eyebrow">YOUR FILES, YOUR DEVICE</div><h1>Privacy, in plain words.</h1><p>Updated 11 October 2026. This page describes the current release.</p><h2>File contents</h2><p>Selected files and pasted content are processed in your browser. These tools do not transmit document contents to a conversion server. We do not store your inputs or outputs between visits.</p><h2>Website requests</h2><p>FilePebble is maintained by Adhi (AdhiAR437 on GitHub) and hosted on Cloudflare Pages at filepebble.com. Your browser downloads the website and its code from Cloudflare. As with other websites, the hosting provider can receive connection information such as your IP address and requested page. Local file processing does not mean that visiting the website is anonymous.</p><h2>No trackers in this release</h2><p>This release includes no third-party analytics, advertising scripts, account system, or tracking cookies. It does not save file contents in browser storage. All application libraries and styles are bundled locally.</p><h2>Markdown preview and downloads</h2><p>Remote images, embedded media, and executable HTML are disabled in previews and exports. Links remain links; opening an external link is your choice and sends a request to that website. PDF printing is handled by your browser and operating system.</p><h2>Local image processing</h2><p>Image tools decode and re-encode selected still images on your device. Exports do not preserve original EXIF metadata. Preview thumbnails and results stay in browser memory and are released when you clear the tool or leave the page.</p><h2>Word export and comparisons</h2><p>Word documents and comparison reports are created locally. Word export omits raw HTML and images, retaining image alt text where available. Supported links remain links; opening them is your choice. Image comparison decodes selected files locally and compares their appearance on a white background.</p><h2>Local PDF processing</h2><p>PDFs are read, transformed and rendered on your device. Rendering fonts, character maps and decoders are served with this website. Previews and outputs remain in browser memory. Selectable-text extraction is available; OCR is not included. PDF page operations do not preserve all document metadata or features and should not be used to remove sensitive information.</p><h2>Updates and contact</h2><p>Before introducing advertising, analytics, payments, or uploaded-file processing, this page will be revised to identify the services used and their data handling. For questions about this page, use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The current contact channel is our public GitHub project; GitHub receives the information you choose to post there under its own terms and privacy policy. Do not include sensitive files or personal information in public reports.</p></article>
  <style>.prose-page a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}</style>
</Layout>
